WEBVTT

00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.190
I've never seen cherry blossoms before!

00:00:13.190 --> 00:00:15.530
They're probably a present 
from the Kingdom of Qi.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.050
They're pretty, but they fall in a week.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:23.500
Claire, good morning!

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:28.300
I'm sorry... I mistook you for someone else.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:31.770
Hey... The first day of school, 
and you're hitting on girls?

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:33.360
It's embarrassing. Stop.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:34.700
It causes problems for me.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:36.510
Hitting on girls?!

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:38.410
I'm not that kind of guy.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.010
You mean you don't have the guts to be.

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:30.580
As planned, we've left 
Balsteros Republic territory.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:34.800
Maintaining a speed of twelve knots, 
in around five months...

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:37.760
We'll reach the legendary Holy Spring.

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:41.900
It's a one-way trip, regardless.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:43.180
It doesn't matter.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:48.510
Provincial Governor Nina Viento, 
and we, the Council of Four,

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:52.310
will oversee the entirety of Isla's 
government. All right?

00:02:54.710 --> 00:02:56.230
But right now, there are only...

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.330
...three of us.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:00.780
That useless idiot!

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:03.240
A famous navigator,

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:06.720
<b>Episode 2 
Cadoques High, Aerial Division</b>

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.670
with a number of awards from

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:06.990
the former Balsteros royal family...

00:03:07.390 --> 00:03:10.010
<i>Is Claire not here?</i>

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:14.140
The chief navigation officer,

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:17.960
Admiral Luis de Alarcon, will now give a speech.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:25.930
We can discuss autographs later.

00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:31.190
Not that I don't enjoy screams of 
pleasure from young ladies...

00:03:33.080 --> 00:03:36.900
Now, for better or worse, Isla has taken off.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:41.150
This is a map of the old world we've left behind.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:47.640
The three continents are occupied solely by 
the nations of Balsteros, Qi, and Benares.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:51.040
And here, the Sauram Sea and the Noel Sea

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.300
are separated from one another by 
an endlessly long waterfall,

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.000
the so-called Great Waterfall.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.720
And around us, the sea stretches on forever.

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:03.890
For many years, this has been the 
entire world humanity has known.

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.440
But six years ago...

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:07.810
The Holy Spring!

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:10.080
A spring in the midst of the vast ocean,

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:13.020
whose existence was foretold in the 
Creation Myth of Saint Aldista.

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:17.820
Oh, and you found it, didn't you, Admiral Luis?

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.570
Yes, as you can see.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:24.200
The legends say

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:29.140
that sometimes, flying islands of 
rock appear from the Spring.

00:04:29.860 --> 00:04:32.070
And that those islands will cross the sea,

00:04:32.070 --> 00:04:36.460
eventually reaching a place, of which we 
know nothing, called the End of the Sky.

00:04:36.890 --> 00:04:39.340
The flying island, Isla, exists.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.170
As does the Holy Spring.

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:44.430
So the End of the Sky must exist, as well!

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:47.350
Each of you is in a different situation.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:50.300
Some of you have come with your families.

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:53.430
Some have left their parents to come here.

00:04:53.780 --> 00:04:56.110
But I hope you'll respect one another,

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:59.860
and will work to improve one another, 
here at Cadoques High.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:04.360
Isla needs you!

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:24.800
Then all these fish came from 
Circular Lake over there?

00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.990
Yep, and not just fish.

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:29.800
In the fields, they raise wheat and vegetables.

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:34.570
I see... then can I have this one?

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:34.890
<i>If I had a pass, I could go to the noble district.</i>

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:40.310
<i>Maybe she caught a cold from falling 
into the lake yesterday.</i>

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:38.280
Here you go.

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:40.310
Thanks!

00:05:40.700 --> 00:05:42.140
What's with you?

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:44.210
You've been acting weird all day.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.010
I guess you're always weird.

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:48.440
You carry it... You're the younger one.

00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:50.780
This again?<i> You're</i> the younger one.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.030
Ah,

00:05:52.430 --> 00:05:55.790
would you like me to carry 
it to the dorms for you?

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.920
Um... Who are you?

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:00.920
Benjamin Sharif.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.310
Sharon Morcoz.

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:03.420
Nice to meet you.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.950
It's a strange system, though.

00:06:07.950 --> 00:06:10.750
Having a different person in charge 
of the cooking each week.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:15.050
Isn't it? What's that dorm manager 
with the bobbed hair thinking?

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:17.030
Are you from Benares?

00:06:17.030 --> 00:06:19.060
You seem to know each other.

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:20.270
Yes.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:22.650
Our houses were adjacent,

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:27.140
and we share, though perhaps involuntarily,

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:29.320
a number of memories.

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:31.120
O-Oh?

00:06:31.590 --> 00:06:35.160
Basically, we're neighbors who've 
been friends since childhood.

00:06:41.770 --> 00:06:42.650
What happened?

00:06:42.650 --> 00:06:43.400
What?

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:44.280
What's going on?

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:45.790
That's Noriaki...

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:47.430
And Nanako Hanasaki.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:49.300
They're from the Kingdom of Qi.

00:06:51.170 --> 00:06:55.680
Truly, commoners should 
learn to behave themselves.

00:06:56.050 --> 00:06:58.460
A-And I apologize...

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:00.470
If you want, I'll wash and return your clothes—

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:01.940
Wai—

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:11.700
Necessary discipline.

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:22.040
Who are you? Are you with them?

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:42.900
Is there still a problem?

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:44.130
You bastard...

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:44.860
Lord Fausto...

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:57.280
Th-Thank you. You saved me...

00:07:57.280 --> 00:07:59.200
You're from our dorm, aren't you?

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:01.120
Wolfgang.

00:08:05.230 --> 00:08:08.270
You're really good, just like a real chef!

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:10.170
We don't have a mom,

00:08:10.170 --> 00:08:14.930
so my sisters and I always traded off on cooking.

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:20.390
Let me see.

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:24.790
You're also really good, Chiharu!

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:25.810
Thanks.

00:08:28.840 --> 00:08:31.860
Don't you think this is a little bland?

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:35.160
W-Wait...

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:37.850
That'll make it too spicy.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:39.870
This is normal for Beneras.

00:08:39.870 --> 00:08:41.140
Hey, stop.

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:42.310
Then a little more—

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:44.750
Is this really going to work?

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:43.000
No.

00:08:45.610 --> 00:08:50.650
By the way, we don't have to make any for that...

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:54.220
You know, the really gloomy, grouchy guy?

00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:58.670
Ignacio Axis.

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:00.680
Don't worry about him.

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:05.140
Shizuka?! Don't eat before everyone else!

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:08.390
I'm sorry. It was just so good.

00:09:09.380 --> 00:09:11.860
Supposedly, he's going to handle his own meals.

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:17.180
The school motto is to nurture your independence.

00:09:17.180 --> 00:09:20.620
Well, I guess that's fine...

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:28.780
Um, how do we sit?

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:32.630
For today, I think the girls and boys 
are just sitting in different places.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:37.300
Time to eat, then!

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:39.640
Let's eat!

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.940
It's so good!

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:52.730
Kal, your sister's amazing!

00:09:52.730 --> 00:09:53.950
Yeah.

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:57.220
Ari's lazy, but she's really good at cooking.

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:57.900
Lazy?

00:09:58.170 --> 00:10:03.630
U-Um... Why did you apply 
to this school, Wolfgang?

00:10:05.830 --> 00:10:07.530
My family is poor,

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:10.490
and I have many younger siblings.

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:14.620
Being a pilot pays better than most jobs.

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:16.520
S-Sorry!

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.520
Don't worry about it.

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:21.410
Just treat me like you would anyone else.

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:24.470
I'm the same age as everyone, 
even if I don't look like it.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:26.390
Eh?!

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:30.750
What about you, Mitsuo?

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:35.080
S-Since I was a kid, becoming a 
pilot's been my dream.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:36.310
Same here! Same here!

00:10:36.310 --> 00:10:38.100
They're so cool!

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:42.120
I'm interested in seeing if the 
End of the Sky really exists.

00:10:42.120 --> 00:10:43.740
And I get ignored?

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.500
So everyone has a good reason to be here?

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:48.830
That's nice.

00:10:49.240 --> 00:10:50.040
What about you?

00:10:50.440 --> 00:10:51.710
Just 'cause!

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.290
Is that not good enough?

00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:56.960
No, it's fine...

00:10:56.960 --> 00:11:00.730
If the End of the Sky really exists, 
that would be wonderful.

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:01.720
Yeah!

00:11:01.720 --> 00:11:03.680
It's so romantic, isn't it?

00:11:05.530 --> 00:11:07.380
Do you think it really exists?

00:11:07.380 --> 00:11:11.320
<i>Isla might be more fun than I expected.</i>

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:16.870
<i>I wonder if I'll be able to see her tomorrow.</i>

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:33.970
He was at the entrance ceremony.

00:11:33.970 --> 00:11:36.590
Seriously? He's our teacher?

00:11:36.910 --> 00:11:39.790
Juan Rodrigo Bandereas.

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:43.840
I'm the man who's going to show you how to fly.

00:11:44.320 --> 00:11:47.970
Call me Mr. Bandereas.

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:50.420
Were you listening?

00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:53.030
"We understand, Mr. Bandereas!"

00:11:53.030 --> 00:11:53.560
Got it?

00:11:53.950 --> 00:11:56.510
We understand, Mr. Bandereas!

00:11:56.510 --> 00:11:57.570
Good.

00:11:57.570 --> 00:12:01.240
I have one more thing to say to you.

00:12:02.890 --> 00:12:05.870
Unfortunately, I overslept this morning.

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:09.750
The nobles in class 1

00:12:09.750 --> 00:12:12.960
should have arrived at the hanger a while ago.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:14.920
In other words?

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:17.760
Run!

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:19.500
As fast as you can!

00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:25.590
I see everyone's here.

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:28.860
But you need more training!

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:34.230
A splendid punch...

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:36.910
You're in top form today, Sonia.

00:12:36.910 --> 00:12:37.900
Of course.

00:12:45.900 --> 00:12:47.770
U-Um...

00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:54.290
Please let me through...

00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.040
I have to hurry—

00:12:57.350 --> 00:12:58.380
Good morning!

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:04.660
I see your blouse is as spotless and 
unwrinkled as ever, Countess Ulshyrra.

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:06.130
Oh, Claire!

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:08.410
You look so wonderful in your uniform.

00:13:08.410 --> 00:13:12.900
I'm sure people will stop and stare, 
as you walk along the road.

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:15.320
Then it's off.

00:13:15.320 --> 00:13:17.730
There's no need for her to attend school.

00:13:18.040 --> 00:13:20.610
No, there is.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.850
It was my decision.

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:27.290
Claire Cruz will attend Cadoques High, Aerial Division,

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:30.700
with the support and guidance of Luis de Alarcon.

00:13:33.540 --> 00:13:36.330
You will keep a strict curfew.

00:13:36.940 --> 00:13:38.280
Hurry.

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:40.340
You're already quite late.

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:42.320
Okay!

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:46.370
There are three curricula at our school.

00:13:46.370 --> 00:13:50.910
The normal curriculum, 
mechanic school, and flight school.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:53.320
I will review this...

00:13:53.320 --> 00:13:57.820
For the next three years, you'll be entrusting 
these machines with your lives.

00:13:58.580 --> 00:14:02.480
This is the El Halcon, a multi-seat trainer.

00:14:02.920 --> 00:14:05.250
7.2 meters long.

00:14:05.250 --> 00:14:07.370
9.33 meters wide.

00:14:07.370 --> 00:14:09.490
3.1 meters tall.

00:14:09.490 --> 00:14:14.610
With a top speed of 350 kilometers per hour and 
a cruising speed of 310 kilometers per hour,

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:16.890
it's equipped with a hydrogen battery stack.

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:17.960
Its engine...

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:22.670
Two Jupiter type-three, air-cooled, 
nine-cylinder radial engines, right?

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:26.710
Who gave you permission to talk?

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:28.690
It's fine...

00:14:28.690 --> 00:14:30.770
Having enthusiasm is good.

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:34.010
Keep it up, and you'll be a full pilot soon.

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:35.490
R-Right!

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:36.930
About that...

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:40.090
Isla is very heavily protected.

00:14:40.090 --> 00:14:41.780
Six fortress cannon platforms,

00:14:41.780 --> 00:14:43.000
the Aerial Knights,

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:45.360
and even a military training school.

00:14:45.810 --> 00:14:51.660
But what, exactly, are these protecting us from?

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.190
An excellent question.

00:14:56.190 --> 00:14:58.790
But for now, shut up and focus on your training.

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:02.880
But it's possible there will be no dogfights at all.

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:11.590
Kal-el...

00:15:17.760 --> 00:15:21.100
We'll pair off for the training flight.

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.270
Pick someone you can get along with.

00:15:23.270 --> 00:15:24.980
Huh?

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:27.040
You have thirty minutes...

00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:27.940
Begin!

00:15:30.620 --> 00:15:31.510
Sharon...

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:33.840
Pair up with me.

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:35.710
Eh? But...

00:15:35.710 --> 00:15:38.660
Supposedly, it's better if 
boys and girls pair up.

00:15:39.220 --> 00:15:41.900
Just give it up, and partner with me.

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:43.880
Oh, fine.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:46.470
Then it's you and me, Nanako.

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:48.710
No, no, no, no! Please, no...

00:15:49.110 --> 00:15:51.310
Want to pair up with me, then?

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:54.010
You're Mitsuo Fukuhara, so I'll call you Mitty.

00:15:54.010 --> 00:15:55.140
Mitty?

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:56.020
Hello!

00:15:56.020 --> 00:15:59.200
I was very moved by the way 
you aided them yesterday!

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:00.500
My name is Marco...

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:02.600
May I call you "brother"?

00:16:02.600 --> 00:16:03.980
Yes.

00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:12.640
Well, he's gonna go with me again.

00:16:15.750 --> 00:16:18.870
Um! I'm sorry I'm late!

00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:33.940
Black hair and that beautiful face...

00:16:33.940 --> 00:16:36.210
Could that be the girl I've heard about?

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:38.930
Yes, it's likely Admiral Luis's...

00:16:38.930 --> 00:16:40.580
I understand.

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:42.560
Very well, then.

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:45.290
As class president, this is my job.

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:47.270
Claire, I finally found you!

00:16:51.750 --> 00:16:53.280
Kal-el, good morning.

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:54.370
Good morning.

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:57.930
From the look of it, you didn't 
catch a cold or anything.

00:16:57.930 --> 00:16:59.200
I'm glad!

00:16:59.970 --> 00:17:03.030
We were just picking partners for training.

00:17:03.030 --> 00:17:05.600
Why don't you pair with me, Claire?

00:17:05.600 --> 00:17:07.040
Wait.

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:10.060
You're the guy from yesterday.

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:14.280
Fausto Fidel Melze.

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:18.180
If you don't know my name, 
you aren't in the Van Whyl class.

00:17:20.170 --> 00:17:22.410
This is Miss Claire Cruz,

00:17:22.410 --> 00:17:24.720
a relative of Admiral Luis.

00:17:24.720 --> 00:17:26.510
You aren't worthy of her.

00:17:27.240 --> 00:17:28.450
Is that so?

00:17:28.450 --> 00:17:32.390
I hear it doesn't matter whether 
you're in class 1 or class 2.

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:35.840
The same nonsense the revolutionary 
government spouts...

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:38.790
A convenient excuse that comes 
from the declaration of equality.

00:17:38.790 --> 00:17:41.830
If you think it actually means 
anything, you're insane.

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:43.450
I understand.

00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:46.850
Then the Melze family was exiled to this island

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:49.580
for not taking it seriously.

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:50.960
Why, you...

00:17:51.380 --> 00:17:54.240
Exiled? What is he talking about?

00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:55.920
And who is that guy?

00:17:55.920 --> 00:17:59.500
The son of Marshal Leopold Melze, 
leader of the knights.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:00.760
What? Seriously?!

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:02.510
That idiot.

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:07.380
Seriously, I shouldn't have expected 
more from the Centezual class.

00:18:07.380 --> 00:18:09.850
I suppose you don't know how etiquette works.

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:13.050
My name is Kal-el Albus.

00:18:13.590 --> 00:18:16.820
And I probably know more 
about etiquette than you.

00:18:26.410 --> 00:18:28.150
Miss Claire Cruz...

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:33.920
Will you fly the clear blue 
skies with me, Kal-el Albus?

00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:45.530
I'm glad...

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:46.890
Thank you.

00:18:51.670 --> 00:18:53.270
Claire Cruz...

00:18:54.210 --> 00:18:56.820
Wait, who am I paired with?

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:11.130
Stay calm.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:12.760
Take your time, and keep steady.

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:14.290
Right!

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:27.930
It's pretty.

00:19:37.710 --> 00:19:40.220
Wow, you're good.

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:42.070
I'll have to do my best, as well.

00:19:43.420 --> 00:19:45.250
Thank you, Kal-el.

00:19:46.830 --> 00:19:51.480
This is the first time someone my 
own age has been so nice to me.

00:19:52.270 --> 00:19:55.210
And it's my first time flying 
with someone like this.

00:19:57.410 --> 00:20:00.030
I'm glad I came to Isla.

00:20:01.730 --> 00:20:05.580
Yeah, so am I...

00:20:15.750 --> 00:20:18.420
Isn't the sky pretty, Mother?

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:21.240
Yes, it really is.

00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:24.970
It's so bright... It's filled with light.

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:28.180
A plane!

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:31.330
Yes... I wonder where it's going.

00:20:31.910 --> 00:20:35.350
Mother, I'm going to learn to fly one.

00:20:35.350 --> 00:20:37.750
I'll fly it... I'll keep flying it forever!

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:41.570
I will learn to fly.

00:20:42.220 --> 00:20:44.720
I'll be a pilot, and fly with you!

00:20:48.110 --> 00:20:49.600
Is that bad?

00:20:53.170 --> 00:20:54.710
That's right, Karl.

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:56.850
Become a pilot.

00:20:57.980 --> 00:21:02.400
Fly free forever, and don't 
let anyone tie you down.

00:21:02.730 --> 00:21:06.240
Fly all the way to the End of the 
Sky, beyond those clouds...

00:21:09.330 --> 00:21:10.220
I will!

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:18.450
Nice job on your first flight, Claire.

00:21:18.450 --> 00:21:21.250
I don't know if I really did it right...

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:23.930
Let's both do our best, as a pair.

00:21:24.550 --> 00:21:25.340
Yes.

00:21:28.170 --> 00:21:30.140
Nice to meet you, Claire.

00:21:32.920 --> 00:21:35.520
But it's strange that you'd choose to pair up

00:21:35.520 --> 00:21:37.770
with someone from the commoner class,

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:40.640
rather than the nobility.

00:21:40.640 --> 00:21:42.230
That's rude, Benji...

00:21:47.610 --> 00:21:50.280
<i>So that's the path you've chosen?</i>

00:21:50.730 --> 00:21:52.300
<i>Kal-el Albus...</i>

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:53.750
<i>No,</i>

00:21:54.110 --> 00:21:56.920
<i>former crown prince of the Balsteros Empire,</i>

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:00.030
<i>Karl La Hire.</i>

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:32.260
I am Ignacio.

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:35.270
School is so boring.

00:23:35.270 --> 00:23:37.430
Curry for dinner?

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:38.930
It isn't my thing.

00:23:38.930 --> 00:23:39.890
Bread's enou—

00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:40.940
<b>Episode 3 
The Wind Revolution</b>
